    "id": "p35-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Solve $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{1}{y^2(y^3-1)^4}$ using the substitution $u=y^3-1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\dfrac{(y^3-1)^5}{15}+C$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}u&=y^3-1\\\\\\frac{du}{dy}&=3y^2\\\\y^2\\,dy&=\\frac{du}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nTaking the reciprocal,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dx}{dy}&=y^2(y^3-1)^4\\\\x&=\\int y^2(y^3-1)^4\\,dy\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting $u=y^3-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac13\\int u^4\\,du\\\\x&=\\frac{u^5}{15}+C\\\\x&=\\frac{(y^3-1)^5}{15}+C.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
